1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,710
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,774 --> 00:00:09,264
A metal spoon sinks.

3
00:00:09,514 --> 00:00:11,404
But a giant metal ship floats!

4
00:00:11,684 --> 00:00:14,234
What is inside the ship that helps it to float?

5
00:00:14,514 --> 00:00:15,454
One, wood.

6
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:16,664
Two, air.

7
00:00:16,944 --> 00:00:18,204
Three, more metal.

8
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:20,360
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:23,182 --> 00:00:24,652
You against the Buddies!

10
00:00:24,912 --> 00:00:26,142
Lock in first.

11
00:00:26,412 --> 00:00:28,222
One finger for every point.

12
00:00:28,512 --> 00:00:30,842
A little otter is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:31,132 --> 00:00:32,332
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:32,911 --> 00:00:34,061
Today you'll learn:

15
00:00:34,263 --> 00:00:35,433
Float or sink.

16
00:00:35,637 --> 00:00:37,057
The material matters.

17
00:00:37,262 --> 00:00:38,822
Why a metal ship floats.

18
00:00:39,469 --> 00:00:40,409
Are you ready?

19
00:00:40,849 --> 00:00:41,619
Three!

20
00:00:41,999 --> 00:00:42,659
Two!

21
00:00:43,029 --> 00:00:43,679
One!

22
00:00:44,099 --> 00:00:44,819
Go!

23
00:00:45,248 --> 00:00:47,058
Two blocks, the same size.

24
00:00:47,328 --> 00:00:48,348
One is wood.

25
00:00:48,658 --> 00:00:49,788
One is metal.

26
00:00:50,088 --> 00:00:51,178
Look closer.

27
00:00:51,830 --> 00:00:53,580
The wooden block bobs up.

28
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:55,380
It floats.

29
00:00:56,730 --> 00:00:58,720
The metal block goes straight down.

30
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:00,440
It sinks.

31
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:03,580
Now two spoons.

32
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:05,750
The wooden spoon floats.

33
00:01:06,330 --> 00:01:07,900
The metal spoon sinks.

34
00:01:11,464 --> 00:01:13,494
Most types of wood float on water.

35
00:01:13,774 --> 00:01:15,524
Most metals sink in water.

36
00:01:16,176 --> 00:01:17,206
Same size.

37
00:01:17,276 --> 00:01:18,186
Same shape.

38
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:19,516
Different material!

39
00:01:20,542 --> 00:01:21,742
Is this the rule?

40
00:01:21,902 --> 00:01:24,292
Heavy things sink, and light things float!

41
00:01:24,494 --> 00:01:26,054
Something is not right.

42
00:01:26,324 --> 00:01:28,504
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

43
00:01:28,784 --> 00:01:29,744
Hold on!

44
00:01:35,257 --> 00:01:36,387
Arms crossed?

45
00:01:36,657 --> 00:01:37,817
One finger up!

46
00:01:38,107 --> 00:01:40,857
The giant ship is very heavy, and it floats.

47
00:01:41,127 --> 00:01:43,367
The little spoon is light, and it sinks.

48
00:01:43,724 --> 00:01:44,934
Here is the rule.

49
00:01:45,133 --> 00:01:46,433
Say it with me!

50
00:01:47,143 --> 00:01:50,523
The material of an object affects the ability of the object to

51
00:01:50,543 --> 00:01:51,933
float or sink.

52
00:01:54,560 --> 00:01:56,060
But a ship is metal.

53
00:01:56,380 --> 00:01:57,700
And metal sinks!

54
00:01:59,009 --> 00:02:01,539
Round one: the question from last time!

55
00:02:01,839 --> 00:02:03,319
What is inside the ship?

56
00:02:03,589 --> 00:02:05,289
Wood, air, or more metal?

57
00:02:05,639 --> 00:02:06,949
Show me your fingers!

58
00:02:10,422 --> 00:02:11,402
Locked in!

59
00:02:11,530 --> 00:02:12,160
One.

60
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,050
Wood floats, so there must be wood inside.

61
00:02:15,103 --> 00:02:15,743
Two!

62
00:02:15,893 --> 00:02:16,493
Air!

63
00:02:16,693 --> 00:02:18,573
My swimming float is full of air!

64
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:19,360
Two!

65
00:02:20,121 --> 00:02:21,271
Look closer.

66
00:02:21,861 --> 00:02:23,901
Here is the giant metal ship.

67
00:02:24,531 --> 00:02:26,411
Part of it sits under the water.

68
00:02:26,762 --> 00:02:28,682
A window opens in its side.

69
00:02:29,262 --> 00:02:30,472
Look inside.

70
00:02:31,092 --> 00:02:32,102
Big rooms.

71
00:02:32,672 --> 00:02:33,902
Tall spaces.

72
00:02:34,552 --> 00:02:35,732
All full of air.

73
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,150
Now the metal block.

74
00:02:38,770 --> 00:02:39,930
Solid metal.

75
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,880
No air inside.

76
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:43,460
It sank.

77
00:02:46,534 --> 00:02:47,834
The answer is two.

78
00:02:48,174 --> 00:02:48,794
Air!

79
00:02:48,899 --> 00:02:49,476
Oh!

80
00:02:49,496 --> 00:02:50,909
Not wood.

81
00:02:50,929 --> 00:02:51,789
Air!

82
00:02:51,996 --> 00:02:53,026
Two fingers?

83
00:02:53,296 --> 00:02:54,516
One finger up!

84
00:02:54,939 --> 00:02:55,879
Be the air!

85
00:02:56,179 --> 00:02:57,149
Shrink down.

86
00:02:57,429 --> 00:02:58,359
Quietly.

87
00:03:00,650 --> 00:03:02,950
You are air, drifting over the sea.

88
00:03:03,624 --> 00:03:07,054
You float in through a door, into a giant metal ship.

89
00:03:07,764 --> 00:03:08,875
A huge room.

90
00:03:08,895 --> 00:03:11,413
Metal walls all around you.

91
00:03:12,327 --> 00:03:13,507
The door shuts.

92
00:03:14,287 --> 00:03:15,557
You are trapped air!

93
00:03:16,217 --> 00:03:18,337
Outside the wall: deep water.

94
00:03:19,187 --> 00:03:20,837
Inside: you.

95
00:03:21,495 --> 00:03:22,925
The ship floats on.

96
00:03:23,725 --> 00:03:24,855
You are helping!

97
00:03:27,066 --> 00:03:28,796
Why does a metal ship float?

98
00:03:29,218 --> 00:03:30,378
Say it with me!

99
00:03:31,084 --> 00:03:33,604
This is because there is a lot of trapped air inside the

100
00:03:33,624 --> 00:03:34,214
ship.

101
00:03:34,854 --> 00:03:37,544
The trapped air helps the ship to float on water.

102
00:03:40,769 --> 00:03:42,229
Now, a metal bowl.

103
00:03:42,619 --> 00:03:43,699
Look closer.

104
00:03:44,054 --> 00:03:45,854
It floats, like a little ship.

105
00:03:46,424 --> 00:03:47,794
Air is inside it.

106
00:03:48,157 --> 00:03:49,627
Now water pours in.

107
00:03:50,227 --> 00:03:52,427
The water takes the place of the air.

108
00:03:52,788 --> 00:03:54,238
The bowl sits lower.

109
00:03:54,848 --> 00:03:55,738
And lower.

110
00:03:56,358 --> 00:03:57,358
It sinks!

111
00:04:01,189 --> 00:04:02,659
Show me your score hand!

112
00:04:02,939 --> 00:04:03,989
More than one?

113
00:04:04,289 --> 00:04:05,649
You beat the Buddies.

114
00:04:05,929 --> 00:04:06,959
Two fingers?

115
00:04:07,229 --> 00:04:08,239
High five!

116
00:04:08,892 --> 00:04:10,332
Did you spot the otter?

117
00:04:10,612 --> 00:04:12,292
It was swimming by the rocks!

118
00:04:12,562 --> 00:04:13,872
Tell someone at home.

119
00:04:14,593 --> 00:04:16,793
Let's read today's key words together!

120
00:04:17,083 --> 00:04:17,843
Ready?

121
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:18,920
Float.

122
00:04:20,172 --> 00:04:20,902
Sink.

123
00:04:22,193 --> 00:04:23,203
Trapped air.

124
00:04:24,658 --> 00:04:25,598
Well done!

125
00:04:26,595 --> 00:04:27,265
Rain!

126
00:04:27,405 --> 00:04:28,925
Oh no, my school shoes!

127
00:04:28,972 --> 00:04:30,452
A plastic raincoat.

128
00:04:30,722 --> 00:04:32,172
A fabric school shoe.

129
00:04:32,452 --> 00:04:33,922
Rain falls on both.

130
00:04:34,192 --> 00:04:36,182
Which one does the water soak into?

131
00:04:36,237 --> 00:04:37,827
Find out in Part Two!

132
00:04:39,187 --> 00:04:40,288
Say it with us!

133
00:04:41,088 --> 00:04:41,838
Ready?

134
00:04:41,961 --> 00:04:42,621
One!

135
00:04:42,961 --> 00:04:43,661
two!

136
00:04:43,966 --> 00:04:45,141
Now you know!
